    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30511" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Naupactus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> ), i, f., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nau-pactum</span></b> , i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ναύπακτος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of
				Ætolia, on the Gulf of Corinth</i>, now <i>Epakto</i> or <i>Lepanto</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				3, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Pis.
				37, 91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 36, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34</span></i> sq.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 2, 3,
				§ 6</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Naupactōus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., Naupactian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Naupactous Achelous,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					2, 43</span></i>
			.</div>
